## KPI Validation and Refinement

During Week 7, the four core KPIs were independently checked against the underlying dataset.

The validated results were:

- Overall No-Show Rate: **48.5%**
- 30+ Day No-Show Rate: **60.5%**
- Repeat No-Show Rate: **55.4%**
- Lost Slot Rate: **53.7%**

A filter-context issue was identified with the **Repeat No-Show Rate** measure.

When the **No prior no-show** category was selected, the KPI initially continued to display **55.4%** instead of responding to the selected filter.

The underlying issue was traced to the original DAX logic, which explicitly filtered appointments using `previous_no_shows > 0`.

The measure was subsequently refined to recognise the selected **Previous No-Show History** context.

After refinement, the no-prior-no-show selection correctly returned:

- No-Show Rate: **43.5%**
- 30+ Day No-Show Rate: **55.2%**
- Repeat No-Show Rate: **0.0%**
- Lost Slot Rate: **49.5%**

The corrected calculation was re-tested successfully.

---

## Key Analytical Findings

### Booking Lead Time

Booking lead time remained the clearest observed pattern in the analysis.

The no-show rate increased across the lead-time bands:

| Booking Lead Time | No-Show Rate |
|---|---:|
| 0–3 days | **24.8%** |
| 4–14 days | **32.6%** |
| 15–30 days | **43.2%** |
| 30+ days | **60.5%** |

This indicates a substantial difference in observed no-show rates across booking lead-time groups, with the 30+ day segment requiring further attention within the analytical context.

### Previous No-Show History

Previous attendance behaviour also showed an observed relationship with appointment no-shows.

| Previous No-Show History | No-Show Rate |
|---|---:|
| Has prior no-show | **55.4%** |
| No prior no-show | **43.5%** |

This provided an additional segmentation variable for understanding appointment attendance patterns.

### Lead Time × Previous No-Show History

A particularly notable segment was the combination of **30+ day booking lead time and previous no-show history**.

Within the 30+ day group:

- Previous no-show history: **67.9% no-show rate**
- No previous no-show history: **55.2% no-show rate**

The overall no-show baseline was **48.5%**.

This interaction was revalidated during Week 7 and remained analytically distinct.

The finding was carried forward as a potential **Lead Time × Previous No-Show interaction feature** for further predictive analysis.

